[?2004hroot@021b4433cb8c:/task# salmon quant --help 2>&1 | grep -A20 -i 'library type' | head -40
[?2004l          Library type (e.g. IU, ISR, A for auto)
          
          [default: A]

  -1, --mates1 <MATES1>...
          Mate-1 FASTQ file(s) for paired-end reads

  -2, --mates2 <MATES2>...
          Mate-2 FASTQ file(s) for paired-end reads

  -r, --unmatedReads <UNMATED>...
          Single-end FASTQ file(s). Mutually exclusive with the paired inputs: supplying both silently quantified only the pairs while `cmd_info.json` still recorded the single-end files, which is the same "wrong mode chosen silently" failure `-a`'s conflict exists to prevent (#1140)

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output directory

  -g, --geneMap <FILE>
          Transcript-to-gene map (GTF/GFF, or a 2-column TSV), optionally compressed (gzip, BGZF, bzip2, xz, zstd); also writes gene-level estimates to `quant.genes.sf`

      --ignoreTxVersion
          Ignore trailing transcript-version suffixes when joining `--geneMap` entries to quantified transcripts, so `ENST00000456328.2` matches `ENST00000456328`. Matches tximport's option of the same name. Needed when the index was built from an Ensembl cDNA FASTA, which carries the version in the identifier, and the annotation is an Ensembl GTF, which puts it in a separate `transcript_version` attribute
--
          Skip transcript quantification (EM + Gibbs/bootstrap) and quant.sf: map (or read the alignments), detect the library type, and write metadata. The run's deliverable is the RAD of the mappings, kept in the output directory; requantify it later with `--rad <file>`. On the default reads path the run stops after mapping, so equivalence classes come from that requant (`--rad <file> --dumpEq`), not from this run. (salmon's --skipQuant)

      --eqclasses <EQCLASSES>
          [not yet implemented] quantify from a previously-written equivalence-class file instead of mapping/alignments (an input mode, not the --dumpEq output)

      --numPreAuxModelSamples <NUM_PRE_AUX_MODEL_SAMPLES>
          Fragments processed before the auxiliary (fragment-length) model is applied during online inference. (salmon's --numPreAuxModelSamples; salmon's default is 1000000, this port's is 5000.) Online-path only (--online, deprecated): ignored with a warning under the default deterministic mode

      --noFragLengthDist
          Disable fragment-length-distribution concordance in the per-fragment probability. Honoured on every quantification path except the deprecated online alignment path (--online -a), which warns that it lacks it

      --noSingleFragProb
          Disable the single-end/orphan fragment-length probability estimate: orphans take a flat penalty instead of the bounded-CMF ambiguous weight, which can change which transcript wins a contested orphan. Honoured on the reads paths and on every RAD-based path (deterministic reads phase 2, -a, --rad). Redundant on the deprecated online alignment path (--online -a), which weights every orphan flat by construction

  -s, --sampleOut
          [accepted; not yet implemented] write a BAM of posterior-sampled alignments (alignment mode)

  -u, --sampleUnaligned
